  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `session_ttl.py`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes.\n\n**Cause:** the function stripped the timezone from `now` but not from `created`. With timestamps like `+00:00`, it then subtracted a timezone-less datetime from a timezone-aware one, and Python raises a `TypeError` for that.\n\n**Fix:** I removed `.replace(tzinfo=None)` so both timestamps are parsed the same way. Timezone-aware inputs are now compared correctly, even across different offsets (for example `+00:00` against `+02:00`). Inputs with no timezone on either side still work as before, and a session under its time limit still returns `False`. I didn't touch `format_expiry_message`.\n\nThe formatter still flags this file, most likely because of a long line that was already there. I left it alone to keep the change to the one-line fix.\n\nDONE: Fixed session_ttl_expired so it no longer strips tzinfo from only the \"now\" timestamp, which made timezone-aware inputs raise TypeError.",
